WEBVTT

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:13.670
 When Chris presented his findings, they were, well, it's nothing new for us.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:18.790
 We have been living through this kind of seasonal hunger for generations.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.790
 We don't call it seasonal hunger.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.790
 We call it Julio, that is July.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:32.790
 And we ask them about, do you have recipes that you use during this period of seasonal hunger that you want to share with us?

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.790
 Almost 800 recipes we collect.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:39.070
 And it's not a lack of knowledge.

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:41.490
 You know, there is a lot of knowledge.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:52.550
 And I think one piece that we try to say, we put together local knowledge, academic knowledge, the NGO, local NGO, international NGO, is all this.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:58.850
 When we start talking about collaboration, you know, it's okay how we put all those pieces together.

